      "writtenOn": "2025-08-27T22:28:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this needed? From what I can tell, it looks like we are only really using it as storage buffers? Or alternatively, should we be adding the uniform one only if the usage contains `wgpu::BufferUsage::Uniform`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 95
      },
      "revId": "5f63ee392cfb7d13984540a5f4eb47e4a432d9fd",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b92be923_f30153bb",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 3954660
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-29T01:19:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the [proposal](https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/texel-buffers.md#vulkan)\n```\nWhen the TEXEL_BUFFER usage flag is set on buffer creation, both of the Vulkan texel buffer bits would be set:\nVK_BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT | VK_BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT\n```\nI read this as: both usages should be added unconditionally. That said, I agree it feels a bit odd, especially since examples of [Vulkan in the wild](https://github.com/LunarG/VulkanSamples/blob/master/API-Samples/texel_buffer/texel_buffer.cpp) seem to set only one usage at a time.",
      "parentUuid": "84e60637_255422d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 95
      },
      "revId": "5f63ee392cfb7d13984540a5f4eb47e4a432d9fd",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ec08945_66c840f4",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/BufferVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 3954660
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-29T01:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, if I’m not mistaken, these usages are mainly for Vulkan device capability checks. I’m not aware of devices that support only uniform or only storage texel buffers, but it seems reasonable to minimize assumptions here, as Vulkan does.",
      "parentUuid": "b92be923_f30153bb",
      "range": {
