      "writtenOn": "2025-08-29T01:19:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this is silently failing when the buffer is destroyed and there’s an API call to create a texel view. That said, this seems to be the expected assumption for functions like this. For example, [TextureVK](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/TextureVk.cpp;l\u003d1938;drc\u003d87c3217dc3fec0f441b68f33d339b7f3a707b11d). I would say that we don\u0027t want to crash the driver, so issuing a no-op command kind of makes sense?",
      "parentUuid": "970ba59a_2cf536fa",
